The records are unmodified; only the surrounding XML was replaced by JSON so a
test can read them. The `openssl_verified` field is not part of the original
data: it is this project's own measurement, recorded with

    openssl 3.6.3 pkeyutl -verify -pubin -inkey <key> -keyform DER \
        -sigfile <signature> -rawin -digest sha256 -in <payload span>

and is used as an oracle independent of the crate under test.

The OCMF specification itself (CC BY-ND 4.0) is *not* redistributed here; it is
fetched into the gitignored `specs/` directory by `cargo xtask spec-sync`.
